his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[1,5,13,14,17,20]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[2,3,8,10,11,13,14,20,21]},{"id":"canaan_914","name":"Canaan","also":"Canaanites, Canaanite","summary":"The fourth son of Ham (Gen. 10:6). His descendants were under a curse in consequence of the transgression of his father (9:22-27). His eldest son, Zidon, was the father of the Sidonians and Phoenicians.","verses":84,"father":"Ham","mother":"","v":[3,7]},{"id":"reuben_2429","name":"Reuben","also":"","summary":"Behold a son!, the eldest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 29:32). His sinful conduct, referred to in Gen. 35:22, brought down upon him his dying father’s malediction (48:4).","verses":70,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[5]},{"id":"simeon_2741","name":"Simeon","also":"","summary":"The second son of Jacob by Leah (Gen. 29:33). He was associated with Levi in the terrible act of vengeance against Hamor and the Shechemites (34:25, 26).","verses":40,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[5]},{"id":"rachel_2386","name":"Rachel","also":"Rahel","summary":"Ewe, “the daughter”, “the somewhat petulant, peevish, and self-willed though beautiful younger daughter” of Laban, and one of Jacob’s wives (Gen. 29:6, 28).","verses":45,"father":"Laban","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[15,16]},{"id":"isaac_616","name":"Isaac","also":"","summary":"The only son of Abraham by Sarah. He was the longest lived of the three patriarchs (Gen. 21:1-3).","verses":123,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Sarah","v":[15,16]}],"places":[{"id":"canaan_272","name":"Canaan","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"The country which derived its name from the preceding. The name as first used by the Phoenicians denoted only the maritime plain on which Sidon was built.","verses":76,"v":[3,7]},{"id":"luz_737","name":"Luz","kind":"City","lat":31.93054,"lon":35.22103,"summary":"The ancient name of a royal Canaanitish city near the site of Bethel (Gen. 28:19; 35:6), on the border of Benjamin (Josh. 18:13).","verses":6,"v":[3]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[5]},{"id":"bethlehem_218","name":"Bethlehem","kind":"City","lat":31.70431,"lon":35.20746,"summary":"A city in the “hill country” of Judah. It was originally called Ephrath (Gen. 35:16, 19; 48:7; Ruth 4:11). It was also called Beth-lehem Ephratah (Micah 5:2), Beth-lehem-judah (1 Sam. 17:12), and “the city of David” (Luke 2:4).","verses":32,"v":[7]},{"id":"ephrath_403","name":"Ephrath","kind":"","lat":31.70536,"lon":35.21027,"summary":"","verses":3,"v":[7]},{"id":"paddan_915","name":"Paddan","kind":"","lat":36.86386,"lon":39.0322,"summary":"A plain, occurring only in Gen. 48:7, where it designates Padan-aram.","verses":1,"v":[7]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[310,310,310,3130,559,559,1,1,2470,2470,3947,3947,3947,3947,5973,8147,8147,1121,4519,669,669],[3290,3290,5046,5046,1121,1121,3130,935,935,413,413,3478,2388,2388,2388,3427,3427,3427,5921,4296],[3290,559,413,3130,410,7706,7200,413,413,3870,3870,776,776,776,3667,3667,1288,1288,1288,1288,853],[559,559,413,